<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Governorate of Paraguay</h1><p class="st-meta">1617 CE – 1811 CE · capital Asunción</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Spanish province centred on Asunción, best known for the Jesuit missions among the Guaraní and for the Comunero revolts against royal authority.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1617 the crown divided the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/governorate-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">Governorate of the Río de la Plata</a> in two. The northern part, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asuncion">Asunción</a>, became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-paraguay">Paraguay</a>, also known as Guayrá, covering the lands along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a> and upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parana-river">Paraná</a> rivers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-paraguay">Paraguay</a> was a poor, largely mestizo and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guarani-people">Guaraní</a>-speaking province. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> built a network of reductions among the Guaraní, which the bandeirantes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a> raided in the 1620s and 1630s, forcing the missions south. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yerba-mate">Yerba mate</a> was the chief export. Settlers resented the Jesuits' control of indigenous labour, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-comuneros-paraguay">Comunero revolts</a> of 1721 to 1735, led at first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-antequera-y-castro">José de Antequera</a>, challenged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>'s authority.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-paraguay">Paraguay</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viceroyalty-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata</a> in 1776 and became an intendancy in 1782. In 1811 it rejected the authority of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-belgrano">Manuel Belgrano's</a> army, and in May overthrew the governor, becoming the independent Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1617 CE – 1811 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South America</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.88%;width:3.86%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1617 CE – 1811 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Asunción</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hernandarias, José de Antequera</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, Guaraní</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/paraguay">Paraguay</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Province of Paraguay, Gobernación del Guayrá</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1714&amp;focus=governorate-of-paraguay" aria-label="Governorate of Paraguay on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3153 3107 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Governorate of Paraguay lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3473 3363L3517 3686M3473 3363L4910 989M3473 3363L3517 3686M3473 3363L3473 3363"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3517 3686h0M4910 989h0M3517 3686h0M3473 3363h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3473 3363h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3473 3363h0"/></svg><